course: dictionary
lesson: 8285
title: Ripen and the -en ending
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To ripen means to become ready to eat, soft and sweet, as fruit does. «As a banana ripens, starch turns into sugar and the skin browns.» Ripen is a verb, so it describes something that happens over time.
explain: The ending -en often means become. Ripe becomes ripen, and wide becomes widen. If you know the small word, you can often work out the longer one. Try it: what does sharpen mean, if sharp means pointed?
explain: Ripen can also mean to make something ripe. «Hard fruit shut in a bag with a ripe banana ripens faster.» Here the ripe banana gives off a gas that makes the other fruit ripen. You can check by swapping in a meaning: «the fruit became ready to eat faster» still makes sense.
explain: A plan or a situation can ripen too. It means it becomes ready or right for action. The word is used in the same way, so you do not need to learn a new meaning. Just look at what is ripening and ask: does it become ready?
fact: To ripen means to become ready to eat, soft and sweet.
fact: Ripen can also mean to make something ripe, or a plan becoming ready for action.
fact: The -en in ripen means become: ripe becomes ripen, and wide becomes widen.
fact: As fruit ripens, its sugar goes up and its acid goes down.
fact: A ripe banana gives off a gas called ethylene, which helps other fruit ripen.
exercise: «As a banana ripens, starch turns into sugar and the skin browns.» What does ripens mean here? | Turns into a bunch of bananas | Gets very cold | *Becomes ready to eat, soft and sweet | Falls off the tree
exercise: «Hard fruit shut in a bag with a ripe banana ripens faster.» What does ripens faster mean? | *Gets ready to eat more quickly | Becomes harder and greener | Turns into a different fruit | Stops growing for ever
exercise: The -en in ripen is like the -en in widen. What does it mean? | Eat | *Become | Green | Ready to bite
test: «Scientists call a tomato a fruit because it holds seeds, and it turns red as it ripens.» What colour does a tomato turn as it ripens? | *Red | Blue | Purple | Black
test: A plan ripens when it becomes ready or right for action. What does ripen mean for a plan? | *Becomes ready for action | Is forgotten by everyone | Gets thrown away | Gets smaller and simpler
exam: Ayesha says ripen means to go bad and rot. Is she right? | Yes, it means to fall off the tree | *No, ripen means to become ready to eat, soft and sweet | No, it means to go to sleep | Yes, ripe fruit always rots
